That means something regenerated 20-nodenet.conf between the two boots.

This is not expected if the node configuration is stable.

I suspect the first reboot happened before networking was fully initialized

The first boot likely generated the node networking drop-ins using an incorrect detected IPv6 address. After the second reboot, when networking came up cleanly, the Machine Config Daemon regenerated the files with the correct addresses.

